The chairman of the board of commissioners shall be authorized to waive any and all bidding requirements for the purchase of necessary materials, supplies, equipment or services under the following circumstances:
(1) Emergency purchases. Whenever an emergency condition exists which presents a threat to the safety, health and welfare of the citizens of the county and whenever such requirements would cause an undue delay in the delivery of essential county services under such conditions;
(2) Cooperative purchasing agreements. Whenever, in the judgment of the chairman of the board of commissioners, it would be in the best interest of the county to enter into cooperative purchasing agreements with other units of government;
(3) State contract purchases. Whenever any item or service is available through a contract with the state and is made available to local governments, and when such items or services meet the requirements of a using agency;
(4) Professional/contractual services. Any necessary function that does not produce a tangible commodity, including, but not limited to, insurance services, leases and rentals, temporary employment, engineering/architectural services, audit and legal services or other services which are by nature not subject to competition; and
(5) Sole source purchase. Any item or service which due to special technology or extraordinary specifications and circumstances, is available from only one vendor.
(Ord. of 4-12-94(1))

